Native reopen repair — focused evidence, not a full acceptance packet
Own source f2691bc2fb4abfe99c50c3cc552e8d6b262ca2f7 on22e596dc; rebased unchanged to4356fc6eea3c7bab3407ed876f9561b26b3a7f41 on0e97dc32.
The final focused run built the unchanged source committed as f2691bc2 during the run. Broader checks on the rebased source are not yet run: QUIET r5i-frame.
Initial failures retained: one missing borrow compiler error; metadata read was wrongly treated as maintenance refresh; expected signer wrongly selected first of two fixture keys. Both test errors corrected without changing native authority, assertions on outcomes, or deadlines.
Final regression checks: Allowed plus typed SQLite DatabaseBusy; public ID hidden; a new Unlock refused; real maintenance refresh retries noninteractive load; one correctly signed completion; exactly one native attempt. All native IO is a mock on a disposable root, no login Keychain.


